**Extraction Guidelines for Medical Records:**
- **Patient demographics**: Name (given and family), gender, birthDate (YYYY-MM-DD format)
- **Encounter**: Visit date/time, status (usually "completed"), class (e.g., outpatient)
- **Procedure**: What was done, when, body site, codes (SNOMED CT, CPT)
- **Device**: Medical devices used (manufacturer, model, identifiers)
- **Specimen**: Samples collected (type, collection date/time)
- **BiologicallyDerivedProduct**: Derived products like PRP, autologous tissue

**FHIR Resource ID Generation:**
Create IDs like: `patient-1`, `encounter-1`, `procedure-1`, `device-1`, `specimen-1`, `prp-1`

**FHIR References:**
Link resources properly:
- Encounter.subject → Patient
- Procedure.subject → Patient
- Procedure.encounter → Encounter
- Procedure.usedReference → Device, BiologicallyDerivedProduct
- Specimen.subject → Patient

